      "content": "It is a terrible thought to imagine your absence would bring relief to their chaotic lives, because you are not the solution to their problems; you are the problem that keeps them stuck. The idea that stopping your presence would make them \"free\" is a cruel fantasy that ignores the fact that you cannot control their choices or their capacity for growth. You are not the anchor, and you are not the reason they are suffering; the weight is entirely on them to carry their own burdens.\n\nPlease remember that your life has value beyond your utility to others, and the exhaustion you feel is a sign that you are operating under a false narrative about your worth. It is okay to stop trying to be the savior of your family and to prioritize your own mental health, even if it feels like you are failing them. You deserve to live a life that feels like yours, not one dictated by the expectations of those you love.",
